SHIORI 1

// ---- Chapter Five: Hinata's point of view, the morning after. -------------------

# sourdough "Sourdough"
@chapter "Chapter Five" subtitle="Hinata"
@pov hinata
@scene bakery with=fade time=2
@filter night time=0
@music small_hours fade=3
@mode nvl
It's four in the morning and I'm making bread, because that's what I do at four in the morning. The oven doesn't care what you're thinking.
Fifty-two. I counted. Every one I've taken up the hill since New Year came home last night, all at once, like starlings into a tree at dusk, shrieking. They're still settling.
Here's one. February, two in the morning, Taichi screaming, the pillow in my hands, and how quiet it would be.
Here's one. The top of the stairs, and Mame on the top step, and how easy.
Here's one. Mother's medicine. Two spoonfuls instead of one. Three. And then I could go to the capital and be a pastry chef, like I say I will in the letters I never post.
Here's the worst one, and it isn't even about hurting anybody. It's just: {i}if they were all gone, I could finally sleep.{/i}
I had these every week. Every Sunday I put them in a glass girl's hands, and walked home singing, and called it feeling like a sponge cake.
@clear
I've tied my apron strings round my wrists. Not tight. Just so I'd notice if my hands went anywhere.
Taichi's asleep upstairs in Mame's bed, because I asked her to take him and she took him without a word. That's the worst part. She just looked at me, and took him.
@clear
@mode adv
mame: You're making the angry bread.
Mame's at the bottom of the stairs in Dad's old shirt, holding Taichi like a sack of rice. He's fussing.
hinata (scared): Mame. Go back up. Take him back up.
mame: He's hungry. I can't do the bottle. You do the bottle.
hinata (tears): I can't.
mame: Yes you can. You do it every night. You did it last night. You just didn't like it.
She puts him in my arms. She has never in her life been afraid of me.
@camera zoom=1.2 time=2
I'm holding him. He's warm and heavy and smells of milk and sleep, and he's fine, he's fine. My hands are doing the bottle by themselves, and not one of the fifty-two is moving them.
It's only a thought. It's only fifty-two thoughts. They're very loud, and I'm still holding him.
@camera reset time=1.5
@if ran_to == "hinata"
  Nagi's asleep on the flour sacks. She went up the hill after I dropped off, and came back before four, and lay down again like a dog that has decided where it lives.
  She carried me home last night. Carried me. I'm a head taller than her. She didn't say a word. She just wouldn't put me down.
  @set hinata_bond += 1
@else
  The bell over the door goes just before five, and it's Nagi, white as flour. She ran after the glass girl last night. Of course she did. I'd have run after her too, if my hands had been mine.
@show nagi tears at=right
Her face is different this morning. Swollen round the eyes, like she's cried for hours. It looks like a house with the lights on.
@if held_baby
  She holds out her arms for Taichi, the way she did on the first morning, and I let her. He stops fussing out of sheer surprise. He always does, with her.
nagi (sad): I remember her, Hinata. The Keeper. Her name is Suzu. She lived two doors down from me, and I gave her away when I was eight.
She tells me in a voice like someone reading a list. A lottery. A row of children. A girl who stepped out of the row.
nagi (sad): What came back? Last night. For you.

* Say the worst one out loud.
  @set said_worst = true
  @set hinata_bond += 1
  My mouth is dry. I say it to the dough, because I can't say it to her.
  hinata (tears): If they were all gone, I could finally sleep.
  It hangs in the kitchen with the flour. Nobody dies. The oven ticks.
  nagi (sad): Mine was: let it be her instead of me. And it was.
  hinata (soft): ...Huh.
  hinata (soft): It's weird how it doesn't kill you. Saying it.
* Say "Nothing much," and keep kneading.
  hinata (tired): Nothing much. Bad dreams.
  She doesn't push. She just stands next to me and kneads, badly, and that's almost worse, because I want to tell her and I can't make my mouth do it.

nagi (resolute): They're drawing lots tonight. In the square. Every child under ten.
I look at Mame, who is eating raw dough and watching us with total contempt.
Mame is eight.
-> changed_town
